  "findings": [
    "Baseline: every HTTP request and the recorder waited for the simulation lock (http p95 1927 ms, max 3550 ms; recorder max 2792 ms). The loop re-acquired the unfair lock after every 0.75 ms step and never slept above ~23x, so SSE frames were seconds apart and GET /api/status took up to 4.0 s -- longer than the dashboard's 1.2 s reconnect-probe timeout, so a dropped stream could not reconnect while overloaded.",
    "Lock contention was only half of it: with the lock removed from delivery, a loop that never blocks still starved other threads of the GIL (33 ms sleep took ~623 ms; command ack ~507 ms). Any blocking call between batches fixes it; 1 ms is the default (see gil_probe and current_yield_0_30s).",
    "Throughput ceiling: arena.step costs ~0.57-0.62 ms and per-step telemetry assembly ~0.17 ms on this host (measured in-process), i.e. <=~27x with per-step telemetry and ~32x without. 100x is not attainable here without faster physics; the daemon now reports achieved speed and 'overloaded'.",
    "20x previously overshot to ~23.7x because the old pacing skipped sleeps under 0.5 ms; deadline scheduling now achieves 20.0x (tests/test_timing_scheduler.py)."
